course: dictionary
lesson: 15702
title: Toothless: no teeth, or no power
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Toothless means having no teeth, or having lost them. «The baby gave a toothless grin.» A baby has no teeth yet, so the grin shows no teeth at all.
explain: Toothless has a second meaning too. «The new rule was toothless, so nobody had to follow it.» Here toothless does not mean without teeth. It means the rule has no real power to make people obey.
explain: Ask yourself: is the thing really about a mouth, or about power? Try your meaning in the sentence. If "no real power to make people obey" still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Toothless means having no teeth, or having lost teeth.
fact: Toothless also means having no real power to make people obey, as in «a toothless law».
fact: Many children have a toothless grin when their baby teeth fall out.
fact: A «toothless watchdog» can bark, but it cannot punish anyone.
fact: Toothless is also the name of a dragon in the film «How to Train Your Dragon».
exercise: «The baby gave a toothless grin.» What does toothless mean here? | *Having no teeth yet | Having no power | Very angry | Very tall
exercise: «The rule was toothless, so nobody had to follow it.» What does toothless mean in this sentence? | Shiny and new | *Having no real power to make people obey | Having lots of teeth | Hungry
exercise: Which phrase means the watchdog cannot punish anyone, not that it has no teeth? | a toothless grin | *a toothless watchdog that cannot punish anyone | a toothless old man | a toothless baby
test: «The old man gave a toothless smile.» What does toothless mean? | *Having no teeth | Clever | Lost in the park | Very loud
test: «The school rule was toothless: teachers could not stop anyone breaking it.» What does toothless mean here? | Had no teeth | *Had no real power to make people obey | Very strict | Very tasty
exam: «The new litter rule was toothless because nobody could be fined.» Which meaning fits best? | Full of litter | *Having no real power to make people obey | Having lots of teeth | Very old and wise
